codex
Two implementation concerns are now concrete enough to drive disposition unless tests disprove them: replay on a later cursor can return the incoming observation ID instead of the already persisted alternate ID, and recovery fsyncs only the literature root after deleting nested files, not each directory whose entry changed. I’m checking whether the scoped tests actually exercise those cases and whether any integrity assertion was weakened.
